  "extraction_notes": [
    "All negative p-channel voltage and current quantities from the datasheet tables and plots are represented as positive magnitudes for model fitting. Curve names and quantity labels retain the published minus-sign semantics.",
    "The datasheet publishes V(BR)DSS = -20 V minimum at VGS = 0 V and ID = 250 uA, IDSS maximum = -1 uA at VDS = -20 V and VGS = 0 V, and IGSS maximum = +/-100 nA at VGS = +/-10 V and VDS = 0 V.",
    "The datasheet publishes RDS(ON) maximum values of 45 mOhm at VGS = -4.5 V and ID = -3 A, and 60 mOhm at VGS = -2.5 V and ID = -2 A. The schema rdson_points records the typical values and conditions.",
    "The datasheet publishes Qg = 6.6 nC typical, Qgs = 0.7 nC typical, and Qgd = 1.4 nC typical at VDS = -10 V and ID = -3 A, with the Qg plot digitized as Fig. 8.",
    "The datasheet publishes ISD maximum = -1.5 A at TA = 25 degC and VSD maximum = -1.2 V at IS = -2 A and VGS = 0 V. No trr or Qrr value is published.",
    "The datasheet publishes RthetaJA = 100 degC/W for a 1 in2 FR-4 board with 2 oz copper, double-sided, in still air at TA = 25 degC. No RthetaJC value is published.",
    "No gate resistance value is published. Switching table values are td(on) = 11 ns, tr = 12 ns, td(off) = 18 ns, and tf = 30 ns at VDS = -10 V, VGS = -4.5 V, ID = -3 A, RG = 3.3 ohm, and RL = 10 ohm.",
    "Figures 6 and 9 are absolute maximum safe operating area and normalized transient thermal impedance plots. They are not transcribed into the generic curve array because their parameterized log-family traces are not required by the mosfet extraction schema.",
    "The transfer figure does not state VDS in its figure annotation. The 25 degC curve was digitized without inventing a VDS condition.",
    "The p. 2 capacitance table explicitly gives Crss = 45 pF typical at VDS = -10 V, VGS = 0 V, f = 1 MHz, which is 4.5e-11 F; the separate 6.6 nC value is Qg, not Crss. Fig. 7 Crss trace was re-checked independently."
  ],
